Core Programming and Frameworks
    Python Programming: Essential for development, data processing, and integration.
    LangChain Framework: Expertise in building, orchestrating DeepAgents and subagents, prompt engineering, and multi-agent workflows.
    Large Language Models (LLMs): Understanding of how to apply and fine-tune LLMs for NLP tasks, reasoning, and decision-making within agents.

Machine Learning & Deep Learning
    Time Series Forecasting: Techniques like LSTM, GRU, Transformers for stock price prediction.
    Natural Language Processing (NLP): Sentiment analysis, text classification, entity recognition to analyze financial news and social media.
    Reinforcement Learning: Basic knowledge to implement adaptive trading strategies.
    Ensemble and Hybrid Models: Combining various prediction models for robustness.

Financial and Stock Market Knowledge
    Technical Analysis: Master technical indicators (RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, moving averages).
    Fundamental Analysis: Analyze financial statements, earnings, ratios, cash flows.
    Market Microstructure: Understand order book dynamics and trade execution strategies.

Data Engineering
    Real-time Data Handling: APIs for streaming stock prices, news, social media data.
    Data Preprocessing & Feature Engineering: Cleaningstock data, extracting meaningful features.
    Database Management: Storing and querying financial and market data.

Software Engineering & DevOps
    API Integration: Connecting multiple data sources and tools.
    Containerization & Cloud Deployment: Docker, AWS/GCP/Azure for scalable deployment.
    Version Control: Using Git effectively.

Visualization & Evaluation
    Data Visualization: Matplotlib, Plotly, or Dash for presenting data and model outputs.
    Model Evaluation: Metrics like RMSE, MAE for predictions, accuracy and F1 for classification.

Optional Advanced Topics
    Graph Neural Networks: For modeling relationships in market data.
    Explainable AI: Interpreting model outputs for transparency.
    Multi-Agent Systems: Designing inter-agent communication and collaboration.
    Prompt Engineering: Crafting LLM prompts specialized for stock market contexts.